{"dog":{"age_group":"adult","application_url":"https://www.nycacc.org/adopt/adoption-process/","availability_detail":"available","breed_display":"Large mixed breed","breed_primary":"Medium Mixed Breed Cross","description_text":"There is an adorable video of me on ACC's TikTok page. Click here to experience the cuteness!\n\nHere's how I've been doing in a foster home! Click here to see!\n\nSince I'm a long stay pup, my adoption fee has been reduced! Visit me today to find out my favorite treats and how you can take me home!\n\nMy foster writes:\nHello all my name is Eggo and im happy that you stopped by to read my bio. I am a 4 year old mixed breed dog and my history is a mystery. I am a loving and caring dog who enjoys learnimg new things, being in the company of others and exploring new places while out on walks. I enjoy eating frozen treats mostly frozen sugar free applesauce, peanut butter and sunflower butter. I also like to have lap time while I watch TV, and letting to audio. I like to play with my toys alone but. im learning how to share. What I REALLY LOVE is Zoomy time!!!!! I get along well with teenagers and adults who have a lot of patience. Once I'm use to you I enjoy tummy rubs and scratches behind my ear.\n\nWhat my friends at ACC say about me:\n\nI have medical needs that staff will address with you when you meet me.\n\nI would appreciate slow introductions to new people and places to help me feel safe.\n\nI would do best in a home without very tiny humans, although I could be open to older human children once I meet them.\n\nI love to be loved, but on my own terms! Let's brush up on some canine body language together!\n\nPlease check here for updated adoption hours.","detail_url":"https://nycaccpets.shelterbuddy.com/animal/animalDetails.asp?s=adoption&searchTypeId=4&animalType=3%2C16&pagesize=75&task=view&tpage=10&searchType=4&animalid=169239","id":"30314b5930b8338fdcf8442368c5adc7","image_urls":["https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/b86d9d3